# Build context for the Dockerfile: sources only. Local build output,
# a developer's runtime state and their cargo overrides stay out — a
# `.cargo/config.toml` patching hx-libs to a local path would break the
# build inside the container. So do secrets: Compose's `.env` files hold
# the first admin password, and the keys a locally-run server writes are
# its identity and its push subscriptions. The build stage copies the
# whole context, so anything left in would sit in its layers.
target/
.cargo/
.git/
.worktrees/
.claude/
accounts/
config.toml
hxd-ng.toml
agreement.txt
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
**/node_modules/
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.key
*.pem
identity-successors/
news-blobs/
